source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-22
observed: A following word rune suppresses the emoticon, so Jira renders the token literally.
-- input.jira --
{{(y)foo}}
-- rendered.html --
<p><tt>(y)foo</tt></p>
-- want.md --
`(y)foo`
-- warnings.json --
[]
